5:/**
6: * SECURE real cross-provider LIFT-AND-SHIFT migration engine (gated behind
7: * ENABLE_REAL_MIGRATION).
8: *
9: * This automates a whole-server move: it copies the selected apps/web roots/home
10: * dirs/Docker data to the SAME absolute paths on the new Nxeon server, dumps and
11: * imports the databases WITHOUT ever asking the customer for a DB password (we
12: * have root SSH into the source, so we dump via root's LOCAL socket/peer auth),
13: * installs the prerequisites the source needs (Docker + compose, DB engines, web
14: * servers, runtimes) from a FIXED package allowlist, brings Docker Compose
15: * projects up, best-effort enables services + web vhosts, then VERIFIES what is
16: * actually running. The final summary honestly separates "migrated & running"
17: * (verified) from "copied — needs a manual step".
18: *
19: * The security bar from the original transfer engine is UNCHANGED and extended:
20: *
21: *   1. STRICT ALLOWLIST VALIDATION. Every non-secret value that is interpolated
22: *      into a command — source host/port/user, file paths, DB engine names,
23: *      Docker volume/compose-dir names, systemd service names, listening ports —
24: *      must match a shell-inert allowlist regex or it is REJECTED (never
25: *      sanitized). The permitted charsets contain no shell metacharacters, so an
26: *      interpolated value cannot break out of the command. Anything that came
27: *      BACK from the untrusted source scan is re-validated here before use.
28: *
29: *   2. FIXED PACKAGE ALLOWLIST. Package installs on the target only ever use
30: *      compile-time-constant package strings from PKG_* below — never a string
31: *      supplied by the source.
32: *
33: *   3. SECRETS NEVER TOUCH A COMMAND STRING. The source SSH password is written
34: *      to a 0600 file over SFTP (bytes, not an argv token) and consumed with
35: *      `sshpass -f`. Database dumps use root's LOCAL auth on each side (unix
36: *      socket / peer), so NO database password exists to leak. DB contents are
37: *      streamed to dump files and never echoed to logs.
38: *
39: *   4. Everything is confined to a per-migration work dir for transient state
40: *      (pass file, known_hosts, DB dumps), bounded by timeouts, and the SSH
41: *      password file is scrubbed in a `finally` block regardless of outcome.
42: *
43: * Best-effort steps (DB dump/import, prerequisite installs, compose up, service
44: * enable, vhost copy) LOG their failure reason and continue — a single failed
45: * sub-step must not fail the whole migration. Only a fatal setup error throws.
46: */
